  "notes": "Surface derived 2026-09-06 and captured VERBATIM: the entire developer-facing surface is three HTMLImageElement additions declared in Chromium's html_image_element.idl — [RuntimeEnabled=UAImageReplacementAPI, Measure] readonly attribute boolean replacedByUserAgent, plus onuareplacestart/onuareplaceend EventHandler attributes — with the event type strings uareplacestart/uareplaceend registered in event_type_names.json5. Five inventory items (1 boolean property, 2 events, 2 handler attributes) map to two stable child routes (replacedbyuseragent/, events/) plus the overview. There is NO formal specification: the ChromeStatus record's spec link is the explainer repository (maturity 'Unknown status'), and the explainer states the proposal 'has not been approved to ship in Chrome' — every page says so. DELIBERATELY PRESERVED AMBIGUITY (explainer: user-agent/feature-specific, not part of the API contract): when replacement occurs, what changes end it, and whether the page is notified at all. The pages document current Chromium behavior (reset on removal from a connected document, document move, or source change out of the replaced original's candidate set; presentation via UA shadow-root iframe; plain non-bubbling non-cancelable Events enqueued as DOM-manipulation tasks) explicitly labelled as implementation tracing, not contract. Events carry no error detail by design — uareplaceend covers finish/fail/revert indistinguishably. Origin trial desktop 152–157 (origin_trial_id 1722063907515793409); no chrome://flags entry (intent: 'no information provided'; runtime feature has no status field, so the Experimental Web Platform features flag does NOT enable it) — enable steps in every warn-block are exact: OT token (header or meta) or --enable-blink-features=UAImageReplacementAPI. No BCD keys, no MDN pages (all 404 2026-09-06), no WPT (intent answers No; wpt.fyi 'uareplace' search empty 2026-09-06), no webstatus.dev/Baseline entry. TAG review: none as yet (Pending). Claimed implementation-sufficient because every declared member is fully documented across all nine dimensions from primary sources and the remaining unknowns are the explainer's own explicit UA-discretion points, preserved as such. Structural validation cannot prove the prose correct; independent primary-source review remains required."
